A||||5||CUTTER||Engine Service Light......whats it mean?||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||05-19-2000||12:31 AM||||I was just cruisen tonight and the light poped on and stayed on till I shut off the car and start driving it, then it comes on a second or two later. Its been doing it all night. I did notice when I was running from some guy that wanted to kick my ass I flew a corner and took it broadside and then the gas peddle was like...glue, It was harder to push then normal and when the auto tranny shifted it would go down in RPM's really slow, like when I slam the gas it shifted at 4000 RPM,s into 3rd it would drop to 2500RPMs really slow. Its like the tranny is screwed up or something, but when I shut the car off and start it back up its fine, except for the "service engine soon" light....what could these things be?<BR>Thanks, Shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||05-19-2000||12:54 AM||||Well let's see. You could have an o2 sensor go out, but again you could have the tpi go bad, but maybe it is the speed sensor, but wait I know it is the map sensor , but again I could be wrong. Why don't you go out and find out the code and maybe somebody will be able to help you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||05-19-2000||03:49 PM||||Fieroshop is right. It only takes 5-10 minutes and about 8 bolts and 2 screws to get at the connector under the center console. Accessing the stored codes takes about another 2 mimutes and leaves no doubt about what the computer thinks is wrong. Beats making guesses and swapping out random parts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||05-19-2000||04:01 PM||||<BR>Hey Larry, not trying to pick on you there bud. But this "It only takes 5-10 minutes and about 8 bolts and 2 screws to get at the connector under the center console" simply is not the case.<P>It will take 30 seconds if you have a torx-20 driver, remove the two torx screws from the cigarette lighter panel, and viola there is the ALDL connector, anything more is disassembeling(sp) the consol which completely unneeded.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||fiero56||05-19-2000||09:58 PM||||Just correcting gold86SE<P>The driver is a t-15(torx) required. Remove the two screw holding on the black cig panel. then paper clip the two brass connections on the lower passenger side. Keys tp "run" then watch the SES light.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LarryB||05-21-2000||04:12 AM||||You're not picking on me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just found its easier for me in the long run to spend the extra couple of minutes and remove the whole console, you have to adapt when the eyes start to go and the tire around the middle gets bigger *lol*<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gold-86SE:<BR><B><BR>Hey Larry, not trying to pick on you there bud. But this "It only takes 5-10 minutes and about 8 bolts and 2 screws to get at the connector under the center console" simply is not the case.<P>It will take 30 seconds if you have a torx-20 driver, remove the two torx screws from the cigarette lighter panel, and viola there is the ALDL connector, anything more is disassembeling(sp) the consol which completely unneeded.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||6
